# Dev server: reuse it, never restart it

The user's dev server runs at http://localhost:3006 under a keep-alive loop (`/tmp/eastwick-dev-3006.sh`, log `/tmp/eastwick-dev-3006.log`) that restarts it if it stops. Other sessions share it.
`next dev` hot-reloads every edit (code, content, CSS, files in `public/`), so a restart is never needed to see a change.

- To check your work, use http://localhost:3006. Do not start another `next dev` in this folder.
- Never `kill`, `pkill`, `lsof -ti:3006 | xargs kill`, or otherwise stop anything listening on 3006, or the loop itself.
- If you need a production check, run `npm run build` and `npm run start -- -p 3010`, then stop only that server.
- If the server is genuinely broken, tell the user and ask before touching it.
